DATA

Files under data/ are released under Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike
4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0), https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/.

Why share-alike rather than CC BY. Sense glosses in the corpus derive in part
from Wiktionary, whose text is dual-licensed CC BY-SA 4.0 and GFDL; share-alike
requires material containing it to carry the same or a compatible licence. The
glosses are not confined to one file: every sense key has the form word::gloss,
so they appear in the labels, the predictions and the key list of every vector
file. Licensing the whole data directory CC BY-SA 4.0 is the simplest way to
comply everywhere at once.

Attribution. Wiktionary content: https://www.wiktionary.org/ and its
contributors, used under CC BY-SA 4.0.

WordNet. Other glosses derive from Princeton WordNet 3.0, whose licence is
permissive and compatible with CC BY-SA, and requires this notice:

  WordNet Release 3.0 Copyright 2006 by Princeton University. All rights
  reserved. THIS SOFTWARE AND DATABASE IS PROVIDED "AS IS" AND PRINCETON
  UNIVERSITY MAKES NO REPRESENTATIONS OR WARRANTIES, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED.

Generated text. Files under data/generations/ and data/generations_single/ are
model output produced under activation steering, included so the analysis can
be reproduced. Some are degenerate, and some are emotionally charged by
construction. They are research artifacts, not endorsed content.

Model weights are not redistributed; models are referenced by Hugging Face
identifier. The NRC VAD Lexicon is not redistributed and no comparison against it
is included.
